    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d170">

                <pb facs="0321" n="221" xml:id="pg221"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A5/18: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Atherton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-01-26T13:00:00+00:00">January 26, 1934—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 26—9:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>16. From Hugh Wilson. Your 16, January 24, 2 p.m. Craigie<anchor n="5"
                        xml:id="d170-f1"/> got in touch with me to inquire whether we had any views
                    as to naval conversations. I followed instructions in your cable and learned
                    from Craigie that the Admiralty also has not yet completed its studies. He had
                    no definite suggestions to make but again reverted to the possibility of his
                    proceeding to Washington en route to visit his wife’s family. Craigie was
                    especially desirous that conversations of a technical nature and very informal
                    and confidential in character should take place at the earliest possible moment
                    after the two Admiralties were ready.</p>
                <p>I did not encourage Craigie in thinking that his visit to Washington would be a
                    procedure which my Government would consider the most advantageous.</p>
                <p>Copy sent Geneva, [Wilson.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Atherton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d170-f1" n="5" xml:id="d170-f1-content">
                <p>Robert L. Craigie, Counselor in the British Foreign Office.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
